+# Release versioning
+
+The user requires an incremented numeric version for every release and its folder/files.
+
+- Current release: 5.13.3. The next patch release is 5.13.4; increment for each new published build.
+- Treat VERSION.txt as the release authority. Keep runtime APP_VERSION, BUILD_NAME, source distribution profile, install marker and installer default consistent with it.
+- Read VERSION.txt in build/launch scripts and workflow artifact names. Pad it to four numeric components for Windows file/product version metadata.
+- Use a fresh source root `WINGO_v<version>` and archive `WINGO_v<version>_FULL_SOURCE.zip`.
+- Include `v<version>` in accompanying release README, validation, checksum, change-list and diff filenames, and publish under `wingo-release/v<version>/`.
+- Preserve previously published folders/artifacts. Verify the archive top-level folder, runtime version, install version and report version all agree before delivery.
+- Stable Python import/entry-point names and installed executable names are runtime contracts; version the release folders and distributable filenames rather than renaming imports.
+- Run the relevant release checks against the exact source being packaged. State Windows compilation and live-broker test limitations accurately.
+- All source versions share the central `<Wingo root>/.env` for broker login. Normal mode is CENTRAL and must not follow stale WINGO_ENV_FILE test overrides.
+- Explicit ISOLATED/EXPLICIT modes require WINGO_ENV_FILE; QA must always opt into ISOLATED with temporary state/credentials and must never fall back to the user's central file.
+- Dhan reads, validates, saves and renews through the same central config authority. Preserve other broker settings and never create per-version credential copies.
+- Dhan PIN/TOTP login uses manually entered six-digit factors once; never load/store factors or TOTP seeds in configuration, logs, mirror snapshots or result metadata. Validate generated tokens against the central client account before replacing saved credentials.
+- Clear Dhan factor widgets on submit, mode change, close, success and failure; keep sensitive HTTP generation details suppressed in standard HTTP logs. Keep FYERS/Upstox broker-page-only OAuth behavior intact.
